Restore the audio.cpp fork's contiguous concat fast paths on the CPU backend
(the fork tags these sites MINITTS_CONCAT_FASTPATH).

Upstream still walks every element scalar-wise, indexing all four dimensions per
element ("TODO: smarter multi-theading"). When src0, src1 and dst are all
contiguous, concatenating along dim 1 is two bulk memcpys per (ne0 x ne1) plane
and along dim 0 is two per row. The framework concatenates per-head attention
outputs in a loop (the ExplicitCpuPerHead lowering in
src/framework/modules/attention/scaled_dot_product_attention.cpp), so this is a
hot path, and losing it in the 0.20.2 convergence was a silent perf regression
rather than a correctness one.

Behaviour is unchanged: the fast paths are gated on full contiguity and fall
through to the upstream loop otherwise.

